## Session summary

**Root cause found and fixed** for the criteria's remaining gap: `mxfs_dlm_bast_work_fn`, `mxfs_dlm_bast_dwork_fn`, and `mxfs_trans_drain_inode_unlocks` (xfs_mxfs_dlm.c) all cleared `ip->i_dlm_demoter = NULL` one statement before their trailing `xfs_irele`/`iput` call. When that ref-drop cascaded into the inode's own synchronous inactivation (MXFS's multi-node destroy_inode path), the nested `xfs_ilock` in `xfs_attr_inactive` no longer saw `demoter == current`, so `mxfs_dlm_ilock_begin`'s wait loop — which explicitly documents "Demoter is exempt (it must re-enter during its own drain)" — treated it as a fresh cross-node request and blocked forever: a self-deadlock. Proven live via `/proc/pid/stack` on a permanently-wedged `mxfs-ino-bast` kworker plus a corroborating kernel `ihold()` WARN_ON on the same PID. Fixed in build 0.10.76 (srcversion `EAB3334D0AA6A8139C0E838`) by moving `demoter=NULL` to after each ref-drop.

**Validated**: `scripts/repro_dblreclaim.sh 8 15 dir_reuse_coherency` completed all 15 iterations with "NO HIT"; the more sensitive P25-INSTR pairing check (new: `scripts/harvest_dblreclaim.sh`) showed 0 dangling/double-entry issues across two real, complete attempts. `fault_netpartition`'s prior FAIL was confirmed to be a pure cascade from the wedge — now passes cleanly (8/8) on a clean cluster.

**Also resolved**: a long, confusing detour chasing what looked like a rival ccloop session fighting for `/tmp/mxfs_run.lock` turned out to be self-inflicted — my own `timeout`-orphaned per-node ssh children (from earlier repro-loop timeouts) inherited the lock's file descriptor via bash's `&` backgrounding. Root-caused, cleaned up, and documented in memory `infra-timeout-orphans-hold-run-lock-not-rival-session`.

**In progress (task #3, the actual exit condition)**: full fresh single-build revalidation sweep of 1/2/4/8/16/32 caw against cutoff `2026-07-13T00:40:00Z` (build 0.10.76). Just launched `scripts/revalidate_cell.sh 1 full` in the background (nohup+setsid, survives session handoff) — log at `/tmp/claude-1000/-src-mxfs/80927ebf-ec69-4017-b901-82ed8c350b63/scratchpad/sweep_1.log`. Remaining: 2, 4, 8 (full), 16 (nodr+dr), 32 (g2+g1+dr), then `python3 scripts/matrix_check.py --since 2026-07-13T00:40:00Z` (no `--nodes` filter) as the final honest gate — must show all six node counts at 17/17 fresh PASS before writing YES.

